			<button name="btnMfPrev5" left="20" top="619" width="50" height="24" text="&lt;&lt;" onClick="mfPage(self, -5);"/>
			<button name="btnMfPrev" left="75" top="619" width="50" height="24" text="&lt;" onClick="mfPage(self, -1);"/>
			<label name="lblMfPage" left="130" top="619" width="260" height="24" horzTextAlign="center"/>
			<button name="btnMfNext" left="395" top="619" width="50" height="24" text="&gt;" onClick="mfPage(self, 1);"/>
			<button name="btnMfNext5" left="450" top="619" width="50" height="24" text="&gt;&gt;" onClick="mfPage(self, 5);"/>

			<button name="btnMfOk" left="390" top="656" width="110" height="24" text="OK" enabled="false" onClick="mfConfirm(self);"/>

			<!-- SPEC I112a/I112b/I112g, Q29 - the description pane. CHILD of mfSearch and not a
			     sibling: a sibling would be a second closing point and the text would outlive the
			     box mfClose hides (V135). The result column does not move one pixel - the box grew
			     to the RIGHT and the pane took the new ground. wordWrap is what kills the horizontal
			     bar here for the same reason it does on edtPopDesc, and there is no field: what
			     leaks to the NDB from the panes is the SIZE, never the text (V29, V334d). -->
			<!-- SPEC I116a/V360a/V360b, pedido 3 do user 2026-08-30. The right half stops being empty
			     space: a rule divides it from the list and a heading names it.

			     The DIVIDER is a sibling of the pane and not a border on it, and that is the point -
			     a border decorates one control, a rule SEPARATES two. It stands at 510, the middle of
			     the 20px gutter between the result column (20..500) and the pane (520..980).

			     The heading is a <label> like every other visible string, so V10 reaches it and the
			     .lang carries `Description` / `Descricao` in both languages. Spelling it in the XML
			     without the [pt] pair is the half-translated sheet V10 refuses. -->
			<rectangle name="mfDescRule" left="510" top="45" width="1" height="635" color="#00000000" strokeColor="white" hitTest="false"/>
			<label name="lblMfDescTitle" left="520" top="45" width="460" height="20" text="Description" horzTextAlign="center"/>
			<!-- SPEC I129d, asks 12 and 13. The pane has TWO states and stays ONE pane: with
			     the Custom line marked these two light up and edtMfDesc drops to top=130; with it
			     unmarked they go dark and the pane goes back to 76/549. Two panes would be two
			     owners of the same text (SPEC V135).
			     Both are born hidden: the box opens on a book entry far more often than on a
			     custom one, and what is authored is the common case. -->
			<label name="lblMfCustomName" left="520" top="71" width="460" height="20" text="Name" visible="false"/>
			<edit name="edtMfCustomName" left="520" top="95" width="460" height="24" visible="false" onKeyDown="escClose(self, event, false);"/>
			<!-- The Revenant row, and it belongs to clanFamily ALONE (SPEC I143d, V413, user
			     2026-09-03). Same shape as the Ritual Level row below and for the same reason: a
			     question the open box asks for ONE list, so the test is on the LIST as well as on
			     the custom state, and neither control owns a field - the answer rides out through
			     MF and nothing here survives the box closing (SPEC V269a, V333e, I129i).
			     It shares the level row's y ON PURPOSE: hedgeRitual and clanFamily are different
			     lists, so the two can never be lit at once, and a second pair of coordinates for
			     the same slot would be two owners of one place (SPEC V135).
			     `values` REPEATS `items` and that is the contract, not laziness: V257c makes the item
			     rebuildable from the value, so the stored token IS the English text and applyLanguage
			     rewrites `items` alone - switching language can never touch what the NDB keeps
			     (SPEC V257b, V257c, V22). `No`/`Yes` already carry PT keys. Authored on `No`: the default is in the FILE and is not
			     written by Lua on open, or it goes missing the day the open path changes (V413c). -->
			<label name="lblMfRevenant" left="520" top="125" width="460" height="20" text="Revenant" visible="false"/>
			<!-- A MARK and no longer a dropdown (SPEC I151d, V437, T979, user 2026-09-06): marked is
			     what `Yes` was and unmarked is what `No` was. The old comment argued `cmb` over `cbo`
			     so the gate would not enrol a two-value enum into the PICKER rules - a mark has no
			     list at all, so that whole question is gone.
			     It is the SAME dot the level row uses two lines down, the prime_on/prime_off pair of
			     V3, so the box does not grow a second vocabulary of marks inside itself. And it is
			     `autoChange="false"` for the same reason those are: the Lua owns the state, so there
			     is exactly ONE writer and the guard in mfRevenantPane is that writer's guard.
			     Authored UNMARKED, which is what `No` was authored as: the default lives in the FILE
			     and is not written by Lua on open, or it goes missing the day the open path changes
			     (SPEC V413c - the widget changed, the reason did not). -->
			<imageCheckBox name="chkMfRevenant" left="520" top="147" width="25" height="25" autoChange="false" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" visible="false" onClick="mfRevenantChange(self);"/>
			<!-- The weakness itself, and it exists only on `Yes`. HIDDEN and not disabled: a control
			     that is invisible and still enabled takes Tab focus, which is the bug no screenshot
			     shows (SPEC V274c, V274d) - the same reason edtClanFamily is authored the way it is.
			     ⚠ the authored text is SHARED with a FLAW of the same name: `Revenant Weakness` is
			     also an entry in PICKER_LIST's flaw list, so this label and that flaw read ONE key
			     in localization.lang and cannot drift apart (SPEC I102g is the same collision one
			     level down, where the cure had to be a composite key because the two meant
			     different things - here they mean the same one).
			     The owner ruled on 2026-09-03: that key goes to `Fraqueza de Revenante`, and its
			     sibling `Revenant Disciplines` with it. `Revenant` alone was the untranslated
			     English, and leaving one of the pair behind would print the same word two ways in
			     one picker list. -->
			<label name="lblMfWeak" left="520" top="177" width="460" height="20" text="Revenant Weakness" visible="false"/>
			<edit name="edtMfWeak" left="520" top="199" width="460" height="24" visible="false" onKeyDown="escClose(self, event, false);"/>
			<!-- T892 piece 1, user 2026-09-01: the Ritual Level row, and it belongs to hedgeRitual
			     ALONE. A homebrew ritual carries no "<n>. " prefix to read a level off, so the level
			     has to be ASKED for; the other eight lists have no level at all, which is why the
			     test is on the LIST as well as on the custom state (SPEC V269b, I129i).
			     Same 25px pitch as the row dots on WoD20.7, so the two read as one widget. They own
			     NO field: they are a question the open box is asking, not data - the answer rides
			     out through MF.level and nothing here survives the box closing (SPEC V269a). -->
			<label name="lblMfLevel" left="520" top="125" width="460" height="20" text="Ritual Level" visible="false"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="chkMfLvl_1" left="520" top="147" width="25" height="25" autoChange="false" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" visible="false" onClick="mfLevelClick(self, 1);"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="chkMfLvl_2" left="545" top="147" width="25" height="25" autoChange="false" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" visible="false" onClick="mfLevelClick(self, 2);"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="chkMfLvl_3" left="570" top="147" width="25" height="25" autoChange="false" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" visible="false" onClick="mfLevelClick(self, 3);"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="chkMfLvl_4" left="595" top="147" width="25" height="25" autoChange="false" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" visible="false" onClick="mfLevelClick(self, 4);"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="chkMfLvl_5" left="620" top="147" width="25" height="25" autoChange="false" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" visible="false" onClick="mfLevelClick(self, 5);"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="chkMfLvl_6" left="645" top="147" width="25" height="25" autoChange="false" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" visible="false" onClick="mfLevelClick(self, 6);"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="chkMfLvl_7" left="670" top="147" width="25" height="25" autoChange="false" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" visible="false" onClick="mfLevelClick(self, 7);"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="chkMfLvl_8" left="695" top="147" width="25" height="25" autoChange="false" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" visible="false" onClick="mfLevelClick(self, 8);"/>
			<imageCheckBox name="chkMfLvl_9" left="720" top="147" width="25" height="25" autoChange="false" checkedImage="images/prime_on.png" uncheckedImage="images/prime_off.png" visible="false" onClick="mfLevelClick(self, 9);"/>
			<!-- SPEC I153a, V439a, ask of 2026-09-06. The three Disciplines a made-up Clan/Family
			     settles, and the block RIDES the Revenant mark: mfCustomPane writes these tops from
			     the SAME base edtMfDesc.top derives from, so the rows sit under the checkbox with the
			     mark off and under the weakness with it on. One cascade, not two (SPEC B70, V413e).
			     The authored tops are the mark-ON position - nothing reads them at runtime, they are
			     here so the file opens on a shape somebody can see.
			
			     The buttons carry no text=: mfLabel writes what the slot holds, or the Select line
			     when it holds nothing, which is why they are dyn* (SPEC V31). -->
			<label name="lblMfClanDisc" left="520" top="237" width="460" height="20" text="Clan Disciplines" visible="false"/>
			<button name="dynMfClanDisc_1" left="520" top="261" width="460" height="24" visible="false" onClick="mfSubOpen(self, 1);"/>
			<button name="dynMfClanDisc_2" left="520" top="289" width="460" height="24" visible="false" onClick="mfSubOpen(self, 2);"/>
			<button name="dynMfClanDisc_3" left="520" top="317" width="460" height="24" visible="false" onClick="mfSubOpen(self, 3);"/>
			
			<!-- The seven cells of a CUSTOM weapon, and they belong to the weapon list ALONE
			     (SPEC I157n, Q77.3, user 2026-09-07 ask 3). The cells on the sheet became
			     read-only in the same batch, so THIS is the only door left for typing one -
			     which is why they live in the pane and not on the tab (SPEC I157k, V460e).
			     Two rows, at the same y the level dots and the Revenant row use: the lists are
			     different, so no two of these groups can ever be lit at once, and a second set
			     of coordinates for one place would be two owners of it (SPEC V135).
			     Born hidden, like every other group in here: the box opens on a book entry far
			     more often than on a custom one, and what is authored is the common case. -->
			<label name="lblMfWpn_roll" left="520" top="125" width="160" height="20" text="Roll" visible="false"/>
			<edit name="edtMfWpn_roll" left="520" top="147" width="160" height="24" visible="false" onKeyDown="escClose(self, event, false);"/>
			<label name="lblMfWpn_diff" left="690" top="125" width="50" height="20" text="Diff." visible="false"/>
			<edit name="edtMfWpn_diff" left="690" top="147" width="50" height="24" visible="false" onKeyDown="escClose(self, event, false);"/>
			<label name="lblMfWpn_damage" left="750" top="125" width="130" height="20" text="Damage" visible="false"/>
			<edit name="edtMfWpn_damage" left="750" top="147" width="130" height="24" visible="false" onKeyDown="escClose(self, event, false);"/>
			<label name="lblMfWpn_range" left="890" top="125" width="90" height="20" text="Range" visible="false"/>
			<edit name="edtMfWpn_range" left="890" top="147" width="90" height="24" visible="false" onKeyDown="escClose(self, event, false);"/>
			<label name="lblMfWpn_rate" left="520" top="177" width="80" height="20" text="Rate" visible="false"/>
			<edit name="edtMfWpn_rate" left="520" top="199" width="80" height="24" visible="false" onKeyDown="escClose(self, event, false);"/>
			<label name="lblMfWpn_clip" left="610" top="177" width="80" height="20" text="Clip" visible="false"/>
			<edit name="edtMfWpn_clip" left="610" top="199" width="80" height="24" visible="false" onKeyDown="escClose(self, event, false);"/>
			<label name="lblMfWpn_conceal" left="700" top="177" width="280" height="20" text="Conceal" visible="false"/>
			<comboBox name="edtMfWpn_conceal" left="700" top="199" width="280" height="24" visible="false"/>
			<!-- The two cells of a CUSTOM armour (SPEC I157o). One row, so the pane closes one
			     step higher than the weapon one does; the notes are the description editor the
			     pane already has, and mfConfirm writes that text to armorDescription as well. -->
			<label name="lblMfArm_rating" left="520" top="125" width="160" height="20" text="Rating" visible="false"/>
			<edit name="edtMfArm_rating" left="520" top="147" width="160" height="24" visible="false" onKeyDown="escClose(self, event, false);"/>
			<label name="lblMfArm_penalty" left="690" top="125" width="160" height="20" text="Penalty" visible="false"/>
			<edit name="edtMfArm_penalty" left="690" top="147" width="160" height="24" visible="false" onKeyDown="escClose(self, event, false);"/>
			<textEditor name="edtMfDesc" left="520" top="71" width="460" height="609" readOnly="true" wordWrap="true" transparent="true" fontSize="12" onKeyDown="escClose(self, event, true);"/>
		</layout>
		<!-- SPEC I153b, V439b/c, ask of 2026-09-06, outcome (b) of Q73. The picker opens OVER
		     the picker: the three Discipline rows in the pane above open a SECOND box, and the
		     first one stays on screen underneath it.
		
		     This is a twin of mfSearch in XML and NOTHING else. Every name is the twin's name
		     plus a B, every left/top/width inside is the same number, and every handler is the
		     same function - one set of mf* functions paints both frames, and mfFound decides
		     which one by MF.depth (SPEC I153c, V439d). Cloning the fifteen functions with an
		     MF2 beside them was the other shape of (b) and it was refused: it would be a second
		     owner of every picker rule there is, and the second copy is the one that ages.
		
		     SIBLING of mfSearch and declared AFTER it, both load-bearing: a child of a 1000x635
		     box the same size would be CLIPPED rather than laid over it, and z-order here is
		     document order, so declared first it would open BEHIND the box that called it - the
		     ask inverted, with nothing raised. It lands at 340,120 - the same 1000x635 shifted
		     forty and forty - so the box underneath shows on both sides and reads as a window.
		     The price of being a sibling is a second frame to hide, and it is paid in ONE place:
		     mfClose at depth 1 hides both (SPEC V439f).
		
		     popScrimB is the scrim twinned with it (SPEC I172b, V503b, 27th batch): every window
		     darkens what is behind it, and behind this one is the first box. Declared BETWEEN the
		     two boxes, so it paints over mfSearch and under this frame, with popScrim's own
		     align/color/opacity (SPEC I181a). mfOpen raises it through the re-keyed `popScrim` at
		     depth 2; a click on it is a click outside THIS box, so it closes this box only (mfClose). -->
		<rectangle name="popScrimB" align="contents" color="black" opacity="0.80" strokeColor="#00000000" visible="false" onClick="mfClose(self);"/>
		<layout name="mfSearchB" left="340" top="92" width="1000" height="695" visible="false">
			<rectangle align="client" color="black" xradius="14" yradius="14" cornerType="innerRound"/>
			<label name="dynMfTitleB" left="60" top="15" width="400" height="20" horzTextAlign="center"/>
			<button name="btnFontDownMfB" left="890" top="15" width="20" height="20" text="-" onClick="fontStep(self, -2);"/>
			<button name="btnFontUpMfB" left="915" top="15" width="20" height="20" text="+" onClick="fontStep(self, 2);"/>
			<button name="btnMfCloseB" left="960" top="15" width="20" height="20" text="X" onClick="mfClose(self);"/>
			<edit name="edtMfQueryB" left="20" top="45" width="480" height="24" onChange="mfConfirm(self);" onKeyUp="mfKey(self);" onKeyDown="escClose(self, event, false);"/>
			<rectangle name="rctMfGameVampireB" left="20" top="77" width="156" height="24" color="DimGray" strokeColor="white" onClick="mfGame(self, 'Vampire');">
				<label name="lblMfGameVampireB" align="client" text="Vampire" horzTextAlign="center" vertTextAlign="center" hitTest="false"/>
			</rectangle>
			<rectangle name="rctMfGameWerewolfB" left="182" top="77" width="156" height="24" color="DimGray" strokeColor="white" onClick="mfGame(self, 'Werewolf');">
				<label name="lblMfGameWerewolfB" align="client" text="Werewolf" horzTextAlign="center" vertTextAlign="center" hitTest="false"/>
			</rectangle>
			<rectangle name="rctMfGameMageB" left="344" top="77" width="156" height="24" color="DimGray" strokeColor="white" onClick="mfGame(self, 'Mage');">
